{
  "slug": "mumo",
  "name": "Mumo",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Multi-model deliberation as MCP tools, with an auto-triggering skill. Consult a panel of models (Claude, GPT, Gemini, Grok, Qwen, GLM, Kimi) on contested decisions where a single model might be confidently wrong, e.g. architecture choices, plan reviews, pricing tradeoffs. Each round returns per-model prose plus a cross-model claim map showing where the panel agrees and where it splits.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, `mumo` (Multi-model deliberation via mumo's MCP server) and **1 MCP server**, `mumo`.\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install mumo@claude-community` from `mumo-chat/mumo-mcp`.\n\nMulti-model responses + cross-model reactions. Want more rounds? Context carries automatically. Stop when you have what you need.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "codex"
  ],
